WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.600
Toki: Vera, “dog bites man” or “man bites dog”. Same thing?

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.523
Vera: Not to you. But attention alone treats the tokens as a set.

00:00:07.923 --> 00:00:10.135
Toki: So if you shuffle us, nothing changes?

00:00:10.535 --> 00:00:15.177
Vera: Every token computes the same result. So each token must be told where it sits.

00:00:16.777 --> 00:00:18.650
Toki: Like a seat number? One, two, three?

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.860
Vera: The original transformer, in 2017, added a fixed pattern of sines and cosines.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.498
Vera: Each row is one position. Each pair of columns is a wave with its own speed.

00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:31.480
Toki: Fast waves on the left, slow ones on the right?

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.872
Vera: Yes. Fast ones tell neighbours apart, slow ones the rough place, like the hands of a clock.

00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:40.016
Toki: Why waves, and not plain numbers?

00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:44.602
Vera: Compare one position's pattern with every other. Neighbours come out most similar.

00:00:45.002 --> 00:00:48.810
Vera: Move from position 20 to 45: the same shape, just shifted.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.436
Toki: So it's how far apart we are, not where we are.

00:00:53.036 --> 00:00:54.722
Toki: Do today's models still add waves?

00:00:55.122 --> 00:01:00.237
Vera: Most use RoPE, from 2021. It rotates pairs of numbers in the query and the key.

00:01:00.637 --> 00:01:04.682
Vera: The angle grows with position: a fast pair, a medium pair, a slow pair.

00:01:05.082 --> 00:01:06.664
Toki: And when two tokens compare notes?

00:01:07.064 --> 00:01:10.983
Vera: Only the difference of their angles survives: relative distance, directly.

00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:14.304
Toki: Does this matter for long documents?

00:01:14.704 --> 00:01:19.627
Vera: Yes. Position is one of the pieces that had to be stretched to make very long contexts possible.

00:01:21.227 --> 00:01:22.365
Toki: Can I play with the waves?

00:01:22.765 --> 00:01:26.779
Vera: Drag the position slider in the Position chapter; Deep mode adds the circles.

00:01:27.179 --> 00:01:28.921
Toki: Found my seat. Now I'm spinning.
